{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness","id":1191090,"title":"Dark Eras for World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-02T12:54:48-08:00","id":1191090,"title":"Dark Eras for World of Darkness","content":"I generally enjoy the Dark Eras series for CoD, but as I'm more a fan of WoD, I've been wondering if the concept would work here as well. (Possibly not so much now that V5 is coming, but one never knows.) Back in the revised days, Ethan Skemp said he'd really like to do a &quot;Kingdoms of the Jaguar&quot; historical book about Mayan era Central America, focusing heavily on the Balam, Mokole, and Camazotz as well as Uktena. I, personally, think this would've been pretty cool. I also really would've enjoyed seeing some sort of &quot;Land of the Setting Sun&quot; KotE sourcebook about Tokugawa Shogunate era Japan and even a 2nd ed Wolves of the Sea covering the Viking Era for all of the Dark Ages lines. <br /> <br /> Any one else have any one-off style historical settings they would have (or even still would) enjoy seeing if possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T13:59:44-08:00","id":1191114,"title":"","content":"Love those ideas - my other picks:<br /> <br /> Dark Ages Wraith is incredibly obvious and badly needed!<br /> <br /> Victorian Age Mage is hopefully still happening<br /> <br /> Bronze Age Collapse Vampire, exploring the possibility of a previous Gehenna set against the Trojan War, the tail end of the Golden Age of New Kingdom Egypt, Book of Jusges Judean, etc etc<br /> <br /> Admittedly, while I love the Classic World of Darkness, this is comparatively harder as the history is less flexible and regional than in Chronicles of Darkness (the trade-off for the big arching global histories that are part of the WoD's flavor)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:21:04-08:00","id":1191123,"title":"","content":"Rage Across the Three Kingdoms seems like it would click well as a concept. It would also help to emphasize the fact that Silver Fangs exist in China by having the Blood Red Crest explicitly noted as being intertwined with the royal Liu clan at the time. Then the fuse to the powder keg starts burning, and the resulting conflicts drag everyone in as their kinfolk are threatened by the state of constant war. And then the banes start to swarm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:41:28-08:00","id":1191129,"title":"","content":"Beast Courts aligning with the Wei/Jin as a response would be interesting (and precede what became of the Garou Nations under the Silver Fangs foothold in China).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:50:38-08:00","id":1191133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191129#post1191129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast Courts aligning with the Wei/Jin as a response would be interesting (and precede what became of the Garou Nations under the Silver Fangs foothold in China).</div> </div> </div> </div>House Blood Red Crest was a more independent operator, according to its blurb in the 2nd edition SF tribebook. I think that they might have been setting them up to be more connected to the Beast Courts, but then anything involving Garou in the Courts became the Hakken Show.<br /> <br /> As for the actions of the courts, technically, they weren't allowed to be a part of human politics so closely. The foxes would be engineering the downfall of officials like Dong Zhuo, though, because it's what they do. And the rats, of course, would be fulfilling their mandated purpose in all of the chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T15:01:22-08:00","id":1191139,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of pieces of lore that allude to happenings there, but I would love to see the World of Darkness's version of Ancient Egypt in its own time, not as a dusty relic. Imagine, the first sparks of the feud between the Setites and the Silent Striders. The birth of the Order of Hermes. The intrigue of the Cults of Thothmes. Insights into the Kingdom of Amenti at the height of its power. Visitors from the Deep Umbra who give their patronage to the Pharaohs in secret. And of course, the conflicts of the ancient gods and their original Undying servants.<br /> <br /> There's so much here it's absolutely dizzying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T05:37:08-08:00","id":1191315,"title":"","content":"I wonder what the Korean peninsula looks like in the WoD\u2019s history. I recall something about the Nagaraja being here... which leaves me perplexed, since I don\u2019t remember there being flesh-eating undead necromancers in our lore. Did they come to reap all the corpses from Imperial Japan\u2019s rule and the Forgotten War that followed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T05:53:36-08:00","id":1191321,"title":"","content":"- Dark Ages Wraith<br /> - KoeT Shogunatu<br /> - Mayan Vampire <br /> - Roma Age Mage<br /> - Rage Across China<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T08:31:39-08:00","id":1191351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191114#post1191114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bronze Age Collapse Vampire, exploring the possibility of a previous Gehenna set against the Trojan War, the tail end of the Golden Age of New Kingdom Egypt, Book of Jusges Judean, etc etc<br /> <br /> Admittedly, while I love the Classic World of Darkness, this is comparatively harder as the history is less flexible and regional than in Chronicles of Darkness (the trade-off for the big arching global histories that are part of the WoD's flavor)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the trick is to try to find a fairly narrow slice of something that plays well with one or two game lines. Say, for example, Antebellum New Orleans drawing on Anne Rice's Feast of All Saints (one of her only non-supernatural novels, dealing with French Creole free people of color) and Arthur Pindle's Bayou St. John, could work well as a Vampire/Wraith/Mage crossover dealing with race relations, voodoo and Los Invisibles. Maybe work in a few Changeling angles as well.<br /> <br /> That Bronze Age period is a fun one. Ten years ago I tried to work out how to do that as a heroic adventure setting for Mutants &amp; Masterminds where Greek heroes, Israelite Judges and others were all around at the same time, but yes, it works really well as a potential Vampire &quot;the world as we know it is ending&quot; setting. If you've never seen George O'Conner's The Olympians graphic novel series, the one on Ares primarily revolves around the Trojan War, with the idea that Zeus engineered the war as a way to get rid of most the god-blooded heroes. I think you could get a lot of milage out of the idea that something devastating to vampires is going on perhaps as a (divinely?) planned way to greatly thin their numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T08:39:52-08:00","id":1191353,"title":"","content":"Bronze Age. I think it fits better with Fae.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T08:40:06-08:00","id":1191354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191139#post1191139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of pieces of lore that allude to happenings there, but I would love to see the World of Darkness's version of Ancient Egypt in its own time, not as a dusty relic. Imagine, the first sparks of the feud between the Setites and the Silent Striders. The birth of the Order of Hermes. The intrigue of the Cults of Thothmes. Insights into the Kingdom of Amenti at the height of its power. Visitors from the Deep Umbra who give their patronage to the Pharaohs in secret. And of course, the conflicts of the ancient gods and their original Undying servants.<br /> <br /> There's so much here it's absolutely dizzying.</div> </div> </div> </div>The War of Horus and Set, sometime after Thoth and Isis have invented True Magic, she and Anubis have returned Osiris from the dead, and Horus has become the first Immortal and is waging his war against the non-dead-yet Set. Primarily Mummy/Vampire with a large dose of Werewolf and a dash of Mage. <br /> <br /> Ptolemaic Egypt, between the death of Alexander and the rise of the Roman Empire would also be pretty cool, with a lot of potential Vampire, Werewolf and Mage hooks including the cult of Hermes-Trismegistus, the Ravnos Alexandrian Jati, and other goodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T08:55:52-08:00","id":1191357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191315#post1191315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what the Korean peninsula looks like in the WoD\u2019s history. I recall something about the Nagaraja being here... which leaves me perplexed, since I don\u2019t remember there being flesh-eating undead necromancers in our lore. Did they come to reap all the corpses from Imperial Japan\u2019s rule and the Forgotten War that followed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nagaraja were an Indian &quot;bloodline&quot; who were a fringe cult of proto-Thanatoics who decided to turn themselves into vampires with Magic. Vampires who enslave and eat the spirits of the dead, and also have to eat human flesh to gain blood, IIRC. In other words, beings who'd become blasphemous fiends by the standards of every human religion and supernatural faction in India. For some reason, the &quot;True&quot; Black Hand let them join, and when that sect collapsed, they decided to ask for sanctuary with the Kuei-jin court in Korea (the Green Court?). That's just about all KotE had to say about Korea, unfortunately. <br /> <br /> This was, of course, nearly 20 years ago, back when Western popular and gamer culture's grasp of East Asia was centered almost entirely on China (kung fu films and Hong Kong action movies) and Japan (anime and ninja/samurai), with everything else (Korea and Vietnam) being Hollywood war movies. Thankfully, this has changed to a degree. <br /> <br /> I think the Silla kingdom in the 6th or 7th century could potentially be a pretty cool setting for KotE, the Beast Courts, Mage and/or the Hsien Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T16:05:58-08:00","id":1191468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191357#post1191357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Silla kingdom in the 6th or 7th century could potentially be a pretty cool setting for KotE, the Beast Courts, Mage and/or the Hsien Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine Kitsune, Gurahl, and Khan dominating the area, with mages of Taoist, Buddhist, and Confucian beliefs. Dunno enough about the Hsien to say anything, and I always thought of Kuei-Jin as the Orientalist splat and not the Asian splat, so off with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T16:12:20-08:00","id":1191470,"title":"","content":"I have sort of mixed feelings about the Kuei-jin. In my own games, I usually prefer just to have Asian counterparts/versions of the existing Clans, adapting their archetypes to places in Chinese, Korean, Tibetan and Japanese culture. The Toreador (and to a lesser extent, the Brujah) I can really see being part of the Hwarang culture, for example, long before the French Courts of the Crimson Rose had ever heard of chivalry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T16:42:41-08:00","id":1191474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191468#post1191468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine Kitsune, Gurahl, and Khan dominating the area, with mages of Taoist, Buddhist, and Confucian beliefs. Dunno enough about the Hsien to say anything, and I always thought of Kuei-Jin as the Orientalist splat and not the Asian splat, so off with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast Courts Gurahl died out in the War of Shame, which would have been before the Xia Dynasty of China. Also, Garou and Fera have a rather mixed compatibility with any given human belief structure, since, as monsters defending the visceral spirit world, they tend to have very inhuman needs, drives, and beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T17:34:13-08:00","id":1191488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191474#post1191474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast Courts Gurahl died out in the War of Shame, which would have been before the Xia Dynasty of China. Also, Garou and Fera have a rather mixed compatibility with any given human belief structure, since, as monsters defending the visceral spirit world, they tend to have very inhuman needs, drives, and beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have long ago kept the Asian Gurahl alive in my games, just because they have such a big place in Korean, Ainu and Chinese myth lore, and I like the idea of animist and Buddhist influenced wilderness priest shaman devoted to the idea of providing Succor for shapeshifters, spirits, people and the land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T17:48:20-08:00","id":1191489,"title":"","content":"I'm pondering the idea of the year 1984 as a Mage setting, but I'd have to work more on specific details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T20:57:06-08:00","id":1191520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191489#post1191489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pondering the idea of the year 1984 as a Mage setting, but I'd have to work more on specific details.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bs0osMzTZQA\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;It's... the... 80s! Do a lot of coke and support the Technocratic Union!&quot;</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T00:58:09-08:00","id":1191568,"title":"","content":"Rage Across India covering Ancient India particularly during King Ashoka's Reign would be my &quot;Take my Money&quot; book! Maybe with something like New Deli by Night for modern India.<br /> <br /> I feel Singapore by Night would be a great setting. A Dubai by Night would be awesome detailing the Glasswalkers and Cainite rivalry under the setting of artificial Islands and Condos owned by world famous sports and movie stars. I guess the Era could be a decade ago when the Island Projects were in full swing.<br /> <br /> And I think the Philippines would be a great setting for a battleground between the Cainites and the Cathayans. An Asian nation with strong Flesh Court powerbase but a heavy influx of Western Kindred over the last couple hundred years. Maybe Mount Pinatubo's erruption and the closing of Clark Airforce base could mark the abandoning of the Philippines by the Cainites to the Flesh Courts. Perhaps it is actually the retreat of the Camarilla, with Sabbat Stragglers trying to keep a grip. Maybe the Volcano was heralding the rise of some ancient Face of the Gods vampire who came from Tamil nobility when they spread to Philippines from India, struggling against mighty Spirit of the Living Earth Ancestors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T17:25:46-08:00","id":1191779,"title":"","content":"Los Angeles: 1984<br /> Mainly for Mage, a sort of New Wave Cyberpunk drawing a lot of influence from The Terminator, Repo Man, The Adventures of Buckaroo Banzai and Streets of Fire, with a bit of Beverly Hills Cop, Dreamscape and the Karate Kid (all from that year) thrown in along with a few bits of stuff like TRON, Poltergeist, and Blade Runner. The Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether are really starting to come into their own as a growing force in the Traditions, and Southern California is a sort of &quot;Wild West&quot; zone of high tech, fringe beliefs, hedonism and suburbia that feels like it could go in any direction. Probably fun as a Changeling setting too. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T17:30:11-08:00","id":1191780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191568#post1191568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage Across India covering Ancient India particularly during King Ashoka's Reign would be my &quot;Take my Money&quot; book! Maybe with something like New Deli by Night for modern India.</div> </div> </div> </div>India during the Gupta Empire (4th to 6th century) would also be a really cool setting for most of the game lines, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T20:16:30-08:00","id":1192130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1191779#post1191779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Los Angeles: 1984<br /> Mainly for Mage, a sort of New Wave Cyberpunk drawing a lot of influence from The Terminator, Repo Man, The Adventures of Buckaroo Banzai and Streets of Fire, with a bit of Beverly Hills Cop, Dreamscape and the Karate Kid (all from that year) thrown in along with a few bits of stuff like TRON, Poltergeist, and Blade Runner. The Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether are really starting to come into their own as a growing force in the Traditions, and Southern California is a sort of &quot;Wild West&quot; zone of high tech, fringe beliefs, hedonism and suburbia that feels like it could go in any direction. Probably fun as a Changeling setting too.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a fun book and with <i>Stranger Things </i>and other shows playing on 1980s nostalgia, something that might work nicely for selling to the non-Mage diehards. You could also mine some of Vampire: New Age Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T08:02:49-08:00","id":1192262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1191090-dark-eras-for-world-of-darkness?p=1192130#post1192130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be a fun book and with <i>Stranger Things </i>and other shows playing on 1980s nostalgia, something that might work nicely for selling to the non-Mage diehards. You could also mine some of Vampire: New Age Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if I was going to suggest a Vampire 80s setting, it's be Miami in the vein of Miami Vice, Scarface, and Body Heat. Possibly with some Wraith and/or Werewolf crossover potential as well. <br /> <br /> For Werewolf, probably New York City influenced by CHUD, Ghostbusters, and Wolfen, with a bit of The Warriors and Death Wish 3 thrown in. <br /> <br /> Wraith would be a one-shot adventure about the ghosts of a bunch of dead teenagers bound to a summer camp trying to stop the Risen that killed them. <br /> <br /> I'm honestly wondering how feasible it'd be to do a Changeling book about the Chicago area suburbs in the vein of John Hughes films. That or Astoria, OR from The Goonies. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T07:05:54-08:00","id":1193912,"title":"","content":"1930s Hollywood for Changeling would be interesting, I think, as would San Fransisco in 1969. <br /> <br /> Also, American Revolution Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> 